      "body": "## Overview\nNotify active request collectors with EngineDeadError when the background output_handler task is cancelled in AsyncLLM.\n\n## Motivation & Behavior Change\n- In Python 3.8+, asyncio.CancelledError derives from BaseException so it bypassed the \\except Exception\\ block in \\output_handler\\.\n- When \\output_handler\\ is cancelled (e.g., during \\AsyncLLM.shutdown()\\ or worker cancellation), active request collectors never received an error notification and remained blocked indefinitely on \\\u0007wait self.ready.wait()\\.\n- **Behavior change**: Pending requests now fail fast with \\EngineDeadError\\ instead of hanging. When shutting down with zero active requests, \\propagate_error\\ is a clean no-op over empty states.\n- Re-raises \\\u0007syncio.CancelledError\\ so the background task cleanly transitions to cancelled.\n\n## Validation\n- Added \\\test_output_handler_cancellation_propagates_to_active_requests\\ in \\\tests/v1/engine/test_async_llm.py\\.\n- Verified code formatting and linting with \\\ruff check\\.\n- Note: End-to-end test execution is validated via Linux CI runners (local machine runs Windows, which lacks native vLLM CUDA extensions and has dependency incompatibilities with transformers 4.57).\n\n## Attribution\nDrafted with assistance from AI pair-programming tools; reviewed, refined, and submitted by human contributor.",
